Girl, Interrupted is a 1999 American biographical drama film directed by James Mangold and written by
Mangold, Lisa Loomer and Anna Hamilton Phelan, based on the 1993 memoir by Susanna Kaysen.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Starring Winona Ryder, Angelina Jolie, Clea DuVall, Brittany Murphy, Elisabeth Moss, Jared Leto, Angela Bettis, Jeffrey Tambor, Vanessa Redgrave, and
Whoopi Goldberg, the film follows a young woman who spends 18 months institutionalized at a psychiatric hospital following a suicide attempt.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Girl, Interrupted was theatrically released in the United States on
December 21, 1999, and grossed $48 million worldwide.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
